<title>JAPAN: Taiheiyo Kouhatsu to develop US coal field.</title>
<headline>Taiheiyo Kouhatsu to develop US coal field.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1996-09-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>Taiheiyo Kouhatsu Inc said on Thursday it had reached an agreement with A.P. Maxwell Development Co of the United States to launch a coal mining project in Colorado.</p>
<p>Taiheiyo has bought half of the mining rights to 17,862 acres of coal field, 32 km west of Trinidad, southern Colorado, for about $1.8 million from A.P. Maxwell, and the two firms have jointly set up Lorencito Coal Co to develop the field, a Taiheiyo official said.</p>
<p>Coal reserves in the field are estimated at around 160 million tonnes, he said.</p>
</text>
